  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements:</p><p>Statement (I) : Planck's constant and angular momentum have the same dimensions.</p><p>Statement (II) : Linear momentum and moment of force have the same dimensions.</p><p>In light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZGleD",
      "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "AYefX",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GzTBr",
      "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vOBtl",
      "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The dimensions of the required quantities can be written as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>ν</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>h</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>E</mi></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>ν</mi></mfenced></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mo>[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>]</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>LT</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mo>[</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>]</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>LT</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mo>[</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>]</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>MLT</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mfenced></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo> </mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>where, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>  is Planck's constant, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is angular momentum, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is linear momentum and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>τ</mi></math> is moment of force.</p><p>From the above analysis, it can be concluded that Statement I is true, but statement II is false.</p>",
